0:{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[[["$","$L2","3.4",{"topic":{"id":"3.4","title":"Social Media Intelligence and Investigations","minutes":13,"summary":"Preserve the account, content, context, and engagement without confusing online persona with verified identity.","sections":[{"title":"What a social-media record should contain","body":["Record the platform, visible account name, stable identifier where available, post URL, capture time, time zone, and surrounding conversation. Display names and usernames can change. A screenshot of only one post may omit edits, replies, quoted content, or a link that explains the statement. Preserve a lawful export or original file when accessible.","Engagement counts are dynamic and can be manipulated. Save the observation time and avoid treating views as unique people or likes as agreement. Public follower lists reveal relationships but not necessarily personal acquaintance. A shared image may be a repost, parody, or evidence of impersonation."]},{"title":"Account control and content interpretation","body":["A post originating from an account does not by itself establish which human used the keyboard. Shared credentials, delegated social-media tools, session theft, and scheduled publishing are alternative explanations. Authentication logs, device records, and witness context may be needed, and non-public records require lawful process.","For threats or harassment, preserve the exact wording, recipient, repetition, and relevant context. Do not amplify intimate or abusive material by circulating it in class. Use redacted presentation copies while retaining the original securely. A platform’s community-rule decision and a court’s legal finding are different determinations."]},{"title":"Collection ethics and provider requests","body":["Use complainant-controlled access or genuinely public material within the authorized scope. Do not send deceptive friend requests or bypass access controls as a classroom exercise. Record why each collected item is relevant, especially where third-party comments contain personal information. Set a retention and access policy.","A preservation request can protect short-lived account records while legal process is arranged. A disclosure request should identify the account and relevant date range precisely. Follow the platform’s lawful-request process and applicable Indian authority. Downloading a profile does not preserve the provider’s underlying logs or deleted backend records."]}],"practice":{"title":"Preserve a changing profile","scenario":"A fictional account repeatedly changes its display name while posting the same payment request.","steps":["Capture the stable identifier and each observed display name.","Save full context and timestamps, not just cropped text.","Separate account-control evidence from content evidence.","Draft a narrow preservation request for relevant provider records."],"debrief":"Stable identifiers, context, and time-aware capture make later analysis more reliable than a folder of unlabelled screenshots."},"terms":[],"lawIds":["it-2021","bnss","bsa"],"sources":["it2026","cert","privacy","bsa"],"labId":"osint","unit":3,"objectives":["Explain what a social-media record should contain and apply it to an investigation.","Explain account control and content interpretation and apply it to an investigation.","Explain collection ethics and provider requests and apply it to an investigation."],"question":{"id":"q-3.4","prompt":"Why preserve a stable account identifier where available?","options":["It conclusively identifies the human operator.","Display names can change, while an identifier may help link records.","It removes the need for context.","It proves every post is true."],"answer":1,"explanation":"An identifier helps connect changing profile records, but account control and human attribution still require evidence.","unit":3}}}]],["$L3"],"$L4"]}],"isPartial":false,"staleTime":300,"varyParams":null,"buildId":"mMiCr23A_-Cpk0hZkfT7X"}
